 removed_case_id  sax susanne 58 f  reg ref 12 23    removed_case_id   wic rooney colleen n p                                                                                             specimen   removed_accession_id   removed_case_id  sout received  12 23 05  removed_case_id  spec type    clinical diagnosis   history  12mm  solid nodule of axillary tail of left breast  fibroadenoma vs cancer edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj gross description  the specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast biopsies  left breast  and consists of five firm  reddish tan needle biopsies with attached blood clot measuring 0 7cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 1 2cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter  5x all  dictated by  lv edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj diagnosis  left breast  axillary tail  needle core biopsies  atypical stromal and epithelial proliferative lesion  see note  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord descriptive comment  note  the biopsies show a fibroepithelial lesion that has stromal hypercellularity and atypia of the stromal cells  the specimen was sent to dr  frederick koerner at massachusetts general hospital  his diagnosis reads as follows   i m afraid that i cannot make a definite diagnosis in this case  the descriptive comment   continued  sections of this core biopsy specimen show a bit of unremarkable breast tissue and a tumor composed of glands embedded in a cellular stroma  the stromal cells strike me as somewhat atypical  certain of them possess one or more large  pleomorphic and hyperchromatic nuclei  the epithelial cells look reactive  they appear enlarged and they contain slightly enlarged nuclei and ample amount of eosinophilic cytoplasm  i suspect that the lesion represents a phyllodes tumor  but i cannot make that diagnosis confidently  i would exclude entities such as fibroadenoma  hamartoma and pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  whose histological features differ from those in the current specimen  an unusual papilloma might display an architecture similar to the one evident in the case at hand  but i must acknowledge that i have never seen a papilloma that looks like this lesion  because of this uncertainty about the diagnosis  i would urge that patient and her physicians to consider an excision of the mass  i suspect that you can make a secure diagnosis after studying the entire nodule   final diagnosis by  nicole a  mihok  m d  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord notes  removed_date  three slides ret d from mgh  jam  cr  removed_date  received letter from mgh dr koerner via fax   mi removed_date  sent all three slides to dr  frederick koerner   mgh via courier for opinion nam jam  co   617  removed_date edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat indm removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjcodes   removed_accession_id    epithelium  nos  removed_accession_id    left breast  no  removed_accession_id    axilla  nos needle  removed_accession_id    axilla  nos atypical breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx lesion  nos breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx proliferation edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dordcopies to  rooney colleen n p  wellesley med  assoc wellesley hills  ma  removed_case_id   781 235  removed_case_id  rubens jami r  m d  radiology department newton  ma  removed_case_id   617 243  removed_case_id markers  breast disease related  presented at breast ca conf   consult case out  consult case return  kodachromes in file edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjprocedures   removed_accession_id   12 29 05  removed_case_id  pat dord  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed